Z||000000||GT Bastard||01-03-2001||09:49 PM||||I'm really interested in attending a driving school.  I started racing auto-x last summer but I want more.  I know I'll need to drive at least a couple hundred miles to do it, but that's fine.  Has anybody had experience with driving schools?  Do they generally run for more than one day?  I'd be looking for one in the midwest(MN maybe.)||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroLisa||01-03-2001||10:23 PM||||I went to a one day driving school but it was more of a "driving experience" with some prior instruction. It was entertaining, and I learned a bit. I can't think of the name off-hand but it was at the Indianapolis Raceway Park. I have a few pics of it on my website, and I will try to come up with the name...<BR><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR>*As Always, Updated Website*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||01-03-2001||10:32 PM||||A driving class is something I have always had on my "things to do this summer" list, but it never seems to get done. The longest I have seen are 3 days lessons, and the shortest are just a few hours(not even worth the $$$ for a few hours), I'd go for 3 days. Maybe this summer. AutoWeek in particular always seems to have certain issues filled with driving classes and locations from all over the country.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||01-04-2001||10:05 AM||||Mid Ohio race course and SCCA/Porsche club sponsor a race course during the spring and summer. They have from 1 day to 3 days. You can drive your own car, so its kinda fun too to see what your car can really do. It does have to have proper safety equipment for you and your instructor, belts, fire ext, ect. I dont have the number but you can go to Mid Ohio in Lexington ohio for their website. If I remember rite, a weekend course is like $1,000. Its really a blast running my replica thru the hairpin and essess at speed.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||01-04-2001||10:52 AM||||my girlfriend took a driving school, in november... of course thatwas to erase a speeding ticket  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>i have always wanted to do a driving school, perhaps now that we have a top notch road course within a hour's drive, i will.<P>hoop||||reg||12
Z||000005||ChadMan||01-04-2001||12:58 PM||||I took Mid-Ohio's one-day High Performance Driving class in 1993.  It was "more fun than a barrelful of halfwitted monkeys" (Foghorn Leghorn).<P>But more importantly, I learned a LOT.  I learned a lot about vehicle dynamics, high-speed cornering, threshold braking, and lots of other great stuff.  I went in cocky, convinced I was already a great driver, and came out humbled after seeing how talented the instructors were.  It's not cheap, though - this class is now $600.  <P>I have no idea how Mid-Ohio compares to other schools like Skip Barber or Bondurant.||||reg||14
Z||000006||Standard||01-05-2001||05:39 AM||||I think there's a Skip Barber driving school at the Brainard International Raceway up north here.  Eventually I'm going to scrape up the money to do that.. ||||reg||
